# Soul SEAL / SEACOM

When the human types **`/seacom`**, `SEACOM`, or `SEAL AND COMMIT`, follow `skills/seacom/SKILL.md`. Interview if needed, then `soul_review_chat_commit` after this run’s picks. Also use `/seacom` for leftover pending items.

When they type `SEAL` or `/soul-seal` only, follow `skills/soul-seal/SKILL.md`. Start-cycle is not a commit. Completing this run’s Review plan picks **is** the commit.

The interview also starts at work-done / subject-finished / before-plan when quarantine is non-empty (see soul-session). Present it as a **Review plan** with several clickable options (Cursor: `AskQuestion`). Start is not a commit. When they pick remember / correct / session_only / reject (or a contradiction set), that **is** approval — `soul_review_chat_commit` immediately. `defer` leaves that item pending. Do not wait for a second slash.

Idle/bye do not commit. Do not run `soul_host`.
